          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Emile Zola</strong><br>\nEmile Zola was born on April 2, 1840, in Paris, France. As a child, Zola's family faced financial difficulties, especially after his father's death when Zola was just seven years old. Despite these challenges, he was able to attend the Lycee Saint-Louis in Paris, although he did not excel in his studies. His early struggle with formal education did not deter his passion for writing, which he began to pursue diligently from a young age.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Beginnings of a Writer</strong><br>\nZola started his career as a clerk in a shipping firm, while writing articles for newspapers on the side. His first book, \"Contes à Ninon,\" was published in 1864, which led to him quitting his job to write full-time. Although his early works were not successful, he persisted, and his dedication soon paid off. By embracing literature, Zola was setting the stage for a prolific career that would include plays, novels, and essays.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Dreyfus Affair</strong><br>\nThe Dreyfus Affair was a significant part of Zola's life, highlighting his courage and commitment to justice. When Captain Alfred Dreyfus was wrongfully convicted of espionage, Zola risked his career to defend him. In 1898, Zola wrote \"J'accuse…!\", an open letter to the French president accusing the government of anti-Semitism and unlawful jailing. This bold move earned him a defamation charge and he had to flee to England to avoid imprisonment.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
